---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell shell--narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="display h2">Why this exists</h1>
      <div class="body" style="margin-top:26px; font-size:1.06rem;">
        <p>Executive education has a structural problem. The university's name is on the
        certificate, but the person teaching is rarely the person who built the thing being
        taught. Programs are delivered by platforms, at scale, by facilitators working from
        someone else's material.</p>
        <p>We started from the other end. Find the people who actually defined a field, build
        a program around them, keep the cohort small enough that participants get real
        access, and put their names rather than an institution's on the work.</p>
        <p><span class="todo">Founding line: who started it, when, and why.</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <section>
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="grid grid--3">
        <div class="card"><h3>Faculty first</h3><p>The program is designed around the person, not the other way round.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Small by design</h3><p>Around thirty seats. Access is the product.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Useful on Monday</h3><p>You leave with a plan for your own organization, not a certificate alone.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>.hero { padding-top: clamp(48px, 7vw, 84px); }</style>
